# gitbulk repo list — one entry per line.
#
# ACCEPTED FORMS (mix freely):
#
#   1. Canonical slug: owner/repo
#        provenant-dev/origin-platform
#      Local clone assumed at <code-root>/<repo-name>.
#
#   2. GitHub URL (HTTPS or SSH): gitbulk parses the slug from the URL.
#        https://github.com/provenant-dev/origin-platform
#        git@github.com:provenant-dev/origin-platform.git
#        ssh://git@github.com/provenant-dev/origin-platform
#      Local clone still assumed at <code-root>/<repo-name>.
#
#   3. Local path: gitbulk runs `git -C <path> remote get-url origin` to
#      discover the slug, AND uses the path itself as the local clone
#      location (overriding <code-root>/<repo-name>). Useful when your
#      clones aren't organized by basename (nested categories, duplicate
#      basenames across owners, etc.).
#        /home/daniel/code/origin-platform
#        ~/code/work/special/nested-clone
#
# REJECTED (these will fail with a friendly error message):
#   - URLs pointing at non-github.com hosts
#   - Paths to directories that don't exist or aren't git repos
#   - Paths to git repos with no `origin` remote
#   - Anything else that can't be canonicalized to owner/repo
#
# OTHER:
#   - Blank lines and lines starting with # are ignored.
#   - Inline comments after #  are stripped.
#   - Duplicate slugs (after canonicalization) → first wins, rest
#     warned + skipped.
#   - Default <code-root> is ~/code/; override per-invocation via
#     `--code-root PATH`.
#   - The `--code-root` override only matters for entries that use
#     forms 1 or 2; form 3 already pins the clone location explicitly.

# Provenant
provenant-dev/origin-platform
provenant-dev/origin-agent-svc
provenant-dev/origin-clerk-svc
provenant-dev/agentprep

